input.script:
export const meta = {
  name: 'zelena-imperija-review',
  description: 'Adversarial multi-lens review of the Zelena Imperija browser game',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Review', detail: 'four independent lenses over the single-file game' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'adversarial refutation of each lens findings' },
  ],
}

const FAJL = '/config/workspace/games/zelena-imperija/zelena-imperija.html'
const SPEC = '/config/workspace/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-02-zelena-imperija-design.md'

const NAODI_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          title: { type: 'string' },
          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },
          location: { type: 'string', description: 'function name or nearby unique code/text snippet' },
          problem: { type: 'string' },
          failure_scenario: { type: 'string', description: 'concrete steps a player takes and the wrong result' },
          fix: { type: 'string', description: 'concrete minimal fix' },
        },
        required: ['title', 'severity', 'location', 'problem', 'failure_scenario', 'fix'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['findings'],
}

const PRESUDA_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    verdicts: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        properties: {
          title: { type: 'string' },
          real: { type: 'boolean', description: 'true only if you FAILED to refute it' },
          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['high', 'medium', 'low'] },
          reason: { type: 'string' },
          location: { type: 'string' },
          fix: { type: 'string' },
        },
        required: ['title', 'real', 'severity', 'reason', 'location', 'fix'],
      },
    },
  },
  required: ['verdicts'],
}

const OSNOVA = `Read the single-file browser game at ${FAJL}.
It is a FarmVille-style cannabis-growing tycoon game. Design spec: ${SPEC}.
All player-facing text is Macedonian Cyrillic; all code identifiers are Latin-transliterated
Macedonian (zasadiSemka, parichnik, presmetajKvalitet). This is deliberate — do NOT report
the Macedonian naming or the Macedonian UI as a problem, and do not suggest renaming to English.
It must stay ONE self-contained file with no external assets, no build step, no network calls —
do NOT suggest splitting it into modules, adding a bundler, or adding dependencies.
Report ONLY concrete defects you can point at in the actual code. No speculation, no style
preferences, no "consider adding tests". If you find nothing real in your lens, return an empty list.`

const DIMENZII = [
  {
    key: 'makedonski',
    prompt: `${OSNOVA}

YOUR LENS: Macedonian language correctness, as a native speaker would judge it.
Check EVERY player-facing string (the TEKST object, the SORTI/NADGRADBI/NASTANI names and
descriptions, the HTML labels, the panel functions, button captions).
Look for: misspellings, wrong grammatical case, wrong verb aspect/form, non-Macedonian words
that slipped in (Serbian/Bulgarian/Russian forms), stray non-Cyrillic characters mixed into
Cyrillic words, awkward or unidiomatic phrasing, and wrong horticultural terminology
(a Macedonian grower's words for germination, vegetative growth, flowering, harvest, drying,
curing, nutrients, pests, mould, spider mites, aphids, yield, strain, potency).
Also verify the strain names built from Macedonian place names are correctly formed
(Скопско Зелено, Вардар Куш, Пелистерска Магла, Охридски Кристал, Шар Планина Хаза,
Дојранска Ноќ) and that lang="mk" content renders as valid Macedonian Cyrillic.
Quote the exact offending string in "location".`,
  },
  {
    key: 'ekonomija',
    prompt: `${OSNOVA}

YOUR LENS: game economy and exploits. Hunt for ways a player breaks or trivialises the game.
Specifically check: can money ever go negative, NaN, or Infinity? Can any action be repeated
for free profit (watering, feeding, treating, harvesting, selling the same batch twice)?
Can the same sushara/magacin batch be processed twice via a double click before the array
splice lands? Are level gates enforced on BOTH the button-disabled path and the function
itself? Can otkluchiLeja exceed MAX_LEI? Can kupiLampa downgrade or be bought twice?
Does XP ever grant an infinite level-up loop? Is there any dominant degenerate strategy
(e.g. never feeding, or harvesting instantly, or holding inventory forever) that beats
playing properly? Does the market drift clamp actually bound the price?
Trace the actual code paths — do not guess.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'js',
    prompt: `${OSNOVA}

YOUR LENS: JavaScript correctness in the browser.
Check: the tick loop and its delta-time catch-up; state mutation during iteration; stale
references after vchitaj() replaces the sostojba object; the dirty-flag panel rendering;
DOM node caching in lejaJazli versus izgradiLei being called again; inline onclick handlers
resolving against globals under "use strict"; SVG attribute vs CSS transform handling;
number formatting with toLocaleString('mk-MK'); localStorage failure paths; the save/load
round trip and field normalisation; any place a NaN or undefined can enter state; event
listener or setTimeout leaks from izvesti(); and whether iscrtajSe() can throw for any
reachable state (empty bed, locked bed, unknown strain, plant at zdravje 0, faza missing).
Report only defects with a concrete reproduction.`,
  },
  {
    key: 'ux',
    prompt: `${OSNOVA}

YOUR LENS: playability, UX and accessibility.
Check: is the core loop discoverable by a new player with no tutorial (do they know to buy a
seed, that drying needs a manual finish, that the market fluctuates)? Are the Сушара and
Магацин tabs reachable and is the player told when something needs attention there? Does the
panel re-render steal focus or reset scroll during play? Colour contrast of the text on the
dark background; are the status bars distinguishable without colour alone; do buttons have
accessible names; is the layout usable at 360px wide and at 1920px; does anything overflow
or overlap; is the 12-bed grid sensible when only 4 are unlocked; can a player get into an
unwinnable state (no money, no seeds, no plants) with no way to recover?
Report only concrete, fixable problems.`,
  },
]

phase('Review')

const rezultati = await pipeline(
  DIMENZII,
  d => agent(d.prompt, { label: `pregled:${d.key}`, phase: 'Review', schema: NAODI_SCHEMA })
        .then(r => ({ key: d.key, findings: (r && r.findings) || [] })),
  (r) => {
    if (!r || !r.findings.length) return { key: r ? r.key : 'nepoznato', verdicts: [] }
    return agent(
      `${OSNOVA}

You are an adversarial verifier. Below are candidate findings from a "${r.key}" review of that
same file. Your job is to REFUTE each one by reading the actual code. Default to refuted:
mark real=false unless you can point to the exact line(s) proving the defect is genuine and
reachable in normal play. Reject anything that is a style preference, a restatement of an
intentional design decision documented in the spec, a suggestion to add dependencies or split
the file, or a complaint about the Macedonian naming convention.
For findings you confirm, restate a minimal concrete fix and a precise "location" string that
uniquely identifies where to apply it.

CANDIDATE FINDINGS:
${JSON.stringify(r.findings, null, 2)}`,
      { label: `proverka:${r.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: PRESUDA_SCHEMA }
    ).then(v => ({ key: r.key, verdicts: (v && v.verdicts) || [] }))
  }
)

const site = rezultati.filter(Boolean)
const potvrdeni = site.flatMap(r => (r.verdicts || []).filter(v => v.real).map(v => ({ ...v, lens: r.key })))
const red = { high: 0, medium: 1, low: 2 }
potvrdeni.sort((a, b) => (red[a.severity] ?? 3) - (red[b.severity] ?? 3))

log(`Potvrdeni naodi: ${potvrdeni.length} od ${site.reduce((n, r) => n + (r.verdicts || []).length, 0)} kandidati`)

return {
  potvrdeni,
  po_leks: site.map(r => ({
    lens: r.key,
    kandidati: (r.verdicts || []).length,
    potvrdeni: (r.verdicts || []).filter(v => v.real).length,
  })),
}

